<p>Russia and Ukraine accused each other on Friday of violating a Russian-declared ceasefire for May 8-10 commemorations of the Soviet victory over Nazi Germany, with both sides reporting new attacks within hours of the truce taking effect. Russia’s Defense Ministry said air defenses downed 264 Ukrainian drones between midnight and 7 a.m. Moscow time, while Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said drones targeted the capital; Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Russian forces had carried out more than 140 strikes on frontline positions and more than 850 drone attacks of various types by 7 a.m. Kyiv time. Moscow had declared the unilateral pause for Victory Day events and warned that any Ukrainian attempt to disrupt the May 9 parade would bring a large missile strike on central Kyiv, while also urging residents and foreign diplomatic missions to leave the Ukrainian capital. Kyiv dismissed the short pause as aimed at protecting the Moscow parade and said Russia had ignored Ukraine’s own ceasefire proposal, which was to begin on May 6. Zelenskyy also warned representatives of states close to Russia against attending the parade, saying Ukraine had received messages that some foreign officials planned to be in Moscow. Russian authorities prepared a reduced Victory Day event, with the BBC and Meduza reporting that Moscow’s parade would be held without tanks or other military hardware and that many regional parades or related marches had been canceled or scaled back.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/dF_7z4Nvisy_uFlun5_uVgTiaWR-04Jfj4L9zIsu7QkpYeknJsh5WKxHYtHNXC7cnIlqnmB7MDJeVE-F5Bhz2BOAl9c5A7PeJ7GvtKdvuqKbCG4mjVIy1GimpcG6SAlEFCaHLfqPN1rcinB9Fp_T7_oL-UIWQmI2qNpY9Xh-HwmAivNFgoI' alt='Russian soldiers ahead of Victory Day commemorations as Moscow prepared for a scaled-down parade.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Air defenses: Ukraine’s air force said it neutralized 56 Russian attack drones overnight.</li><li>Russian sites: Regional officials in Rostov reported damage from drone debris, and officials said the Urals region of Perm was attacked with drones.</li><li>Ceasefire terms: The Russian Defense Ministry said its ceasefire covered frontline operations and long-range strikes on Ukrainian military and infrastructure targets tied to the war effort.</li><li>Security measures: Reports described heightened security around the Moscow celebrations, including mobile internet disruptions linked to concerns about Ukrainian drones.</li></ul><blockquote>On the Russian side, there was not even a token attempt to cease fire on the front - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine: President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Russia appeared to want Ukraine’s permission for a one-hour Red Square parade before returning to the war, and said Ukraine would answer Russian attacks in kind. (<a href='https://kyivindependent.com/we-dont-recommend-zelensky-warns-foreign-officials-against-attending-russias-victory-day-parade/'>Kyiv Independent</a>)</li><li>Russia: Russia’s Defense Ministry said it was observing the May 8-9 pause and accused Kyiv of breaching it with drone attacks, saying Russian forces would respond to violations. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639582-russia-victory-day-ceasefire/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Foreign diplomats in Kyiv: Diplomats in Kyiv told the Kyiv Independent they were not moving after Russia urged foreign missions to leave the capital before possible Victory Day retaliation. (<a href='https://kyivindependent.com/russia-warns-embassies-to-flee-kyiv-before-victory-day/'>Kyiv Independent</a>)</li><li>Kremlin adviser Yuri Ushakov: Ushakov said Russia had not issued special invitations to foreign dignitaries for this year’s Victory Day parade, while reports listed officials expected to attend. (<a href='https://stirileprotv.ro/stiri-externe/singurul-lider-european-care-va-merge-la-parada-lui-putin-lista-oficialilor-prezenti-la-moscova-de-ziua-victoriei.html'>Știrile ProTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3